WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.277
The third condition asks whether at least one abnormal lab exists.

00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:10.167
Because we only need one qualifying related row, EXISTS is the natural contract.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:15.477
Run the query and identify the patients that satisfy this part of the practice problem.

00:00:15.477 --> 00:00:19.597
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:19.597 --> 00:00:24.402
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:24.402 --> 00:00:27.777
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:31.577
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:31.577 --> 00:00:38.027
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:38.027 --> 00:00:43.927
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:43.927 --> 00:00:46.080
not only whether the statement executes.
